package anyimage

// Plan 45, against the real images (opt-in like recipes_live_test.go, never
// the server's Docker):
//
//   COSMOS_FORK_LIVE_DOCKER=1 DOCKER_HOST=tcp://<dind>:2375 LIVE_HUB_MIRROR=mirror.gcr.io \
//     go test ./src/anyimage/ -run 'RecipesLive(Login|Managers)' -v   (ONLY=postgres,pgadmin narrows it)
//
// TestRecipesLiveLogin: every recipe with a login is started with a password
// generated by its rule at the rule's maximum length, holding every class
// the rule allows (both cases, digits, each of its symbols), and the
// username the rule makes of "Owner.Name"; then each account signs in for
// real (the database's own client in a container of the same image on a
// network of the test's own, or HTTP to a port the Docker in Docker
// publishes), and a wrong password is refused.
//
// TestRecipesLiveManagers: a database and its manager on a network only the
// two share (names resolve by container name, as Cosmos sets them up), a
// table or key made in the database, then a scripted session with the
// manager signs in and must show that table or key.
//
// Passwords travel only in environment variables, never on a command line.

